TY  - CPAPER
ID  - CWC-F44066254E0A
TI  - Validation of Numerical Model for Simulation of Drilling Discharges to Sea
AU  - Henrik Rye
AU  - Edgar Furuholt
PY  - 2010
T2  - Abu Dhabi International Petroleum Exhibition and Conference
DO  - 10.2118/137348-ms
UR  - https://doi.org/10.2118/137348-ms
AB  - Abstract The site survey for the location of the Trolla exploration well in the Norwegian Sea revealed numerous potential locations of cold water corals. These corals are expected to be vulnerable for sedimentation of particles and exposure to chemicals from drill cuttings and drilling fluids. How vulnerable they are for these disturbances is, however, not well known. Numerical simulations were performed to predict spreading of drill cuttings and drilling fluids, including concentrations in the water column and sedimentation on the seabed. A monitoring program was also conducted, comprising cuttings particle size measurements, current measurements, sediment traps collecting depositing particles, sediment sampling, turbidity measurements and video observations. The monitoring program gave the possibility to compare results from the numerical model with observed deposition of drill cuttings. The simulation results showed good correspondence with the contents in the sediment traps, supporting the validity of the numerical model.
